    "clm-apss-applications-app03": {
      "text": "Marlowe builds financial contracts from a small number of constructs, accounts and continuations. The authors describe Isabelle proofs for semantic properties, including money preservation and a timeout after which an empty transaction closes a contract and returns account funds. The proof translation differs from Haskell in identifier and map representation.",
